  "details": "In Project Settings > Physics, the Default Material is not applied to colliders with none applied.\n\nAccording to its tooltip, it should apply to all colliders with no physics material applied.\n\nBut it doesn't.\n\nDuring testing, I made a very bouncy material for checking.\n\n- If I apply a physics material manually to a collider, it works and will bounce as expected.\n\n- But if I set it to none on the collider, and then set the same material as the Default Material in settings, it would not be applied to the collider. The collider will behave as if no physics material is applied.",
